- How would you adapt to additional languages and more features?
- How would you handle severe class imbalance or drift over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical detection of AI-generated content with model attribution, latency constraints, multilingual support, and robust auditing in a live chat setting.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time on-device + cloud inference
- AI-generated content detection and model attribution
- Per-post explainability and tamper-evident auditing
- Drift detection and privacy-preserving processing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo on-device scorer and cloud orchestrator
function scorePost(post) {
  const local = localModel.predict(post.text);
  if (local.confidence > 0.6) return {flag: true, score: local.confidence, method:'local'};
  // fallback to cloud for deeper check
  return CloudService.analyze(post).then(r => ({flag: r.flag, score: r.score, method:'cloud'}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle multilingual coverage and language drift over time?
- What metrics and rollback plan would you use for production calibration and user impact assessment?

